WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.056
What you've just seen is more than a new way to use a bank.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.061
It raises a bigger question.

3
00:00:05.693 --> 00:00:15.810
As personal AI assistants become more capable, customers may turn to them first to compare mortgages, manage savings, arrange protection, and plan their financial future.

4
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.037
And those assistants won't necessarily belong to banks.

5
00:00:19.635 --> 00:00:27.283
If somebody else owns the conversation, they may gain the context, shape the recommendations, and influence where the customer's loyalty sits.

6
00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:35.603
The bank could still provide the products, hold the balance sheet, and carry the regulatory responsibility, while someone else shapes the experience.

7
00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:45.016
Saoirse explores how we can respond: by building a direct conversational relationship, and connecting securely to the assistants customers choose to use.

8
00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:48.022
So, who will customers choose to talk to?

9
00:00:48.343 --> 00:00:51.450
Try Saoirse yourself, or read the thinking behind it.
